{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787234408,"nonce":"e3uij0cqUydg7u/1rEo2GNu4Iwk=","title":"**What is wrong.** `state_version` is a component of every §C.7 notification idempotency key, and","message":"`enqueueNotify` writes the literal `1` for every evaluation — so the component discriminates nothing\non the Case path. `internal/alerts/service/service.go:443` is `StateVersion: 1` inside the\n`jobs.NotifyEvaluateArgs` literal, and `mint` floors a zero at `1`, so no notification about a Case\nhas ever carried a version other than 1.\n\n**The demonstration.** `alert_cases.state_version` exists and is maintained: added by\n`db/migrations/00023_occurrence_occ.sql:16`, documented by `00052_the_firing_episode_is_a_case.sql:236`\nas *\"Optimistic lock. Every state transition is a compare-and-set on this value; a lost CAS is a\nconflict, never a silent overwrite.\"*, read by `Case.StateVersion()`\n(`internal/alerts/domain/case.go:152`), and `CaseRepository.Transition` refuses a CAS that does not\nname it. Nothing reads it into the notification path. The wire that used to exist was\n`alert_groups.state_version`, and it was deleted with the table — `service.go:429`'s ⚠️ block records\nexactly this.\n\n**Why it matters.** The pin it implements is what stopped a late enrichment from resending an older\nstate (§C.7). With the version constant, two facts about one Case at different states can only be\ntold apart by their Reason, so the pin is unenforced. The digest path is unaffected — `digest.go`\npasses its window ordinal — so this is specifically the Case path.\n\n**Why this is NOT urgent, and why it is filed anyway.** Wiring it re-keys every `fired`, `acked`,\n`all_resolved` and `enriched` notification, which changes *which pairs of facts collapse into one\ncard*. That is a behaviour change across the whole product, not a bug fix, and it is why commit\n`8b56e45` deliberately left it alone: it also would not have fixed the re-snooze case that commit\naddressed, because a snooze attaches to the Alert and moves no Case lock, so the real column would\nhave read `1` there too.\n\n**Where.** `internal/alerts/service/service.go:443` (the literal) and `:429` (the ⚠️ record) ·\n`internal/notification/service/notify.go` (`mint`, the key) · `internal/alerts/domain/case.go:152` ·\n`db/migrations/00023_occurrence_occ.sql:16` · `db/migrations/00052_the_firing_episode_is_a_case.sql:236`\n· SPEC §C.7.\n\n**Scope.** medium\n\n**Done when.** **Owner ruling, 2026-08-20: `state_version` stays hard-coded for now** and the\ndecision is recorded in SPEC §C.7 rather than left as a code comment, so a reader of the spec learns\nthe pin is not enforced on the Case path. This ticket then stays open as the record of the unwired\npin. Wiring it later requires: a golden vector pinning a literal §C.7 digest FIRST (nothing in CI\ncurrently pins one, so a pre-image change is silent), then reading the real column, then a decision\nabout what collapse behaviour is wanted for the four reasons above.","files":null}]}